spans.s:
√sādh (sā́dhati, -te; sā́dhitum; sādháyati
).
 —1. come straight to one's aim,
attain one's object;
 —2. bring straight to
one's object; --caus.
 —1. bring to its
object or end; accomplish;
 —2. attain,
win. [cf. √2sidh, ‘succeed.’]

sādhú, f. sādhvī́, a.
 —1. leading straight
to the goal; straight (path), 83^17;
 —2.
good or noble (of people); faithful (wife),
64^10; as m. noble man, 21^19; as f. excellent
woman, 46^7;
 —3. as adv. right;
regularly, 86^12; well; as excl. bravo ! 14^22,
48^16. [√sādh, 1178a.]
